# Code Style Rules for rTorrent Project

## TypeScript Guidelines
- Use TypeScript with strict typing
- **NEVER** use `any` type - always provide proper types
- Use meaningful variable and function names
- Follow existing code patterns and conventions

## XML-RPC Handling
- Handle XML-RPC responses carefully with proper error handling
- Use `fast-xml-parser` for XML parsing
- Implement proper fault handling for XML-RPC errors
- Handle case-insensitive hash comparisons

## rTorrent API Conventions
- Follow rTorrent XML-RPC API conventions
- Implement proper deletion sequences when available
- Add appropriate delays for torrent operations
- Use proper XML-RPC method names

## Error Handling
- Implement proper error handling for all API calls
- Use try-catch blocks for operations that might fail
- Provide meaningful error messages
- Log errors appropriately

## Documentation
- Add JSDoc comments for public methods
- Include links to rTorrent documentation where possible
- Document XML-RPC method names and parameters
- Explain complex logic with comments
